      "raw": "I mean, if we're going to be exacting about it, the length of a single solar revolution varies from \"year\" to \"year\" anyway (we lose about .0055 seconds each time IIRC) and a \"day\" is a pretty arbitrary unit of measurement - and that's not even considering the whole \"leap year\" kludge we've got going on.  \n\nI'm sure Tachyon notices this stuff, a fraction of a second is a usable period of time for her.  :)\n\nAlternately, the cake has nothing to do with the passage of time, and GLaDOS is trying to recruit you for a study.  Might want to be wary of portals for a while.",
